  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_4' aria-label=\" Indian Railways versus West Bengal State Electricity Distribution Company Limited & Ors. pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('4','2026','2026_5_479_521','2026INSC464'); ><font size='4'> <strong>INDIAN RAILWAYS<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>WEST BENGAL STATE ELECTRICITY DISTRIBUTION COMPANY LIMITED & ORS. </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 5 S.C.R. 479</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 464</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010001552026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : DIPANKAR DATTA<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, SATISH CHANDRA SHARMA</strong><br> Issue for Consideration The specific issues which arise for determination are: (i) Whether the activities provided u/s.11(g) and (h) of the Railways Act pass muster of &ldquo;distribution&rdquo; of electricity, and whether such activities are a necessary pre-requisite to the Act; (ii) Whether the Indian Railways, being an entity of the Central Government, falls within the ambit of &ldquo;Appropriate Government&rdquo; u/s.14 of the Electricity Act, 2003; (iii) Whether the Indian Railways, even if held to be a DDL under the Act, is exempt from the obligation to<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 08-05-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CIVIL APPEAL No. 4652/2024</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Dismissed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('4','2026','2026_5_479_521','2026INSC464','S')><i <i class='fas fa-column